 \n- Liat Berdugo (Media Artist) on "Technologies of the Surface: Embodying
  the Gestural Interfaces of Everyday Technology"\n\n- Julia Markel on "Whi
 ch self does AI remember?"\n\n- Vinod Menon (Professor of Psychiatry & Beh
 avioral Sciences) on "The Default Mode Network\, the Self\, and Consciousn
 ess in the Age of AI"\n\nLiat Berdugo is a multidisciplinary artist and wr
 iter whose work investigates the relationship between technology\, visuali
 ty\, politics\, and power. She is an Associate Professor of Art + Architec
 ture at the University of San Francisco. Her work has been exhibited in th
 e USA\, Europe and Australia. Her book\, The Weaponized Camera in the Midd
 le East\, was published in 2021. Along with Emily Martinez\, she is one ha
 lf of the art collective\, Anxious to Make\, and is the co-founder of the 
 Living Room Light Exchange\, a monthly new media art series.\n\nJulia Mark
 el is currently a final-year PhD student in Computer Science at Stanford\,
  advised by James Landay. Her research interests are in human-computer int
 eraction with a focus on human-centered AI. She is currently working on pr
